# D3: lexical blocks - a name made in a block is the block's, and a name outside it with the same
# spelling is another variable; the loop counter hides the `i` declared before it. No `vars`
# inside the loop: the outer `t` is in scope there and not yet set, in Shalimar and in C alike.
break @:5
break @:10
break @:12
run
print i
print t
continue
continue
print i
print t
continue
vars
print t
print u
continue
vars
print i
print t
continue
